<div class="prose series-introduction"><p>CyberAlchemy is a system for organizing knowledge and work. Definitions state the meanings and boundaries on which explanations and assessments depend. Once an accountable owner accepts an exact version within a declared scope, it supplies <strong>authority over meaning</strong>. The Lab calls that formal acceptance <strong>admission</strong>.</p><p>Let’s follow an agent investigating an incident involving a data extraction. It needs an accepted completeness criterion and permission for the particular investigation. The same incident continues through the provenance and lifecycle articles.</p></div>
<section class="article-section" id="incident-case" aria-labelledby="incident-case-heading"><h2 id="incident-case-heading">An incident to investigate</h2>{{INCIDENT_CASE}}</section>
{{VISUAL_AUTHORITY}}
<section class="article-section" id="authority-surfaces" aria-labelledby="authority-surfaces-title"><h2 id="authority-surfaces-title">Applying the meaning to work</h2>
{{AUTHORITY_CONTEXT}}
</section>
<section class="article-section" id="authority-agent" aria-labelledby="authority-agent-title"><h2 id="authority-agent-title">What an agent needs before acting</h2>
<div class="prose"><p>An <strong>Agent Assignment</strong> identifies the investigation Work item. A <strong>Delegation</strong> records permission for specified actions, subjects and time limits. Here the authorized service owner permits session {{CASE_SESSION}} to inspect Northstar’s saved material, compare identifiers and prepare candidate assessment and change proposals within its recorded window. Deployment and incident closure require authority for those effects.</p></div>
<h3 class="article-subheading">The agent’s checks</h3>
<ol class="series-process" aria-label="How accepted meaning informs work"><li><strong>Find the governing version</strong><p>Identify the accepted definition and applicable rules for this task’s scope.</p></li><li><strong>Use them in a specific assessment</strong><p>Apply the completeness criterion to the declared snapshot, using the required method and permitted tools.</p></li><li><strong>Record what happened</strong><p>Save the result and its sources. Review a proposed fix through the authority route for that change.</p></li></ol>
<h3 class="article-subheading">How accepted meaning informs later work</h3>
<div class="prose"><p>A definition can influence a schema, validator, task view or later decision through explicit bindings. The implementation and the observed effect must be identifiable too. Accepting a definition does not itself execute software, change a database or authorize every action connected to the subject.</p></div>
<p class="series-bridge">The next question is how to trace the result to the information and work that produced it.</p>
{{SOURCES_AUTHORITY_AGENT}}
</section>
